"description":"Syracuse has ruled starting quarterback Steve Angeli out for Saturday's game against Notre Dame due to a shoulder injury.","published":"2026-11-23T18:40:45.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50575118/syracuse-rules-qb-steve-angeli-shoulder-vs-notre-dame","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Indiana not yet naming starting QB for game vs. Purdue, Curt Cignetti says","description":"Indiana is not yet naming a starting quarterback for Saturday's rivalry game against Purdue, coach Curt Cignetti said Monday.","published":"2026-11-23T18:51:39.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50575086/indiana-not-yet-naming-starting-qb-game-vs-purdue","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Alabama's Kalen DeBoer expects QB Keelon Russell to be 'full go' vs. Auburn","description":"Alabama coach Kalen DeBoer said Monday that he expects QB Keelon Russell, who is working his way back from an ankle injury, to be \"full go\" for rivalry week against Auburn.","published":"2026-11-23T18:13:53.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50574915/alabama-deboer-expects-qb-russell-full-go-auburn","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5197086/sahir-west","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sahir_West"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Sahir West","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sahir_West","description":"American football player","touched":"2026-11-14T07:37:28Z","intro":"Sahir West is an American college football defensive lineman for the UCLA Bruins. He previously played for the James Madison Dukes.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"West attended Mount Saint Joseph High School in Baltimore, Maryland. As a junior, he totaled 63 tackles, ten sacks, and an interception. Following his high school career, West committed to play college football at James Madison University."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"West played sparingly in 2024, appearing in two games and earning a redshirt. His production increased the following season, recording ten tackles, 5.5 tackles for loss, and three sacks in the 2025 Sun Belt Conference Football Championship Game against Troy. At the conclusion of the regular season, West was named the Sun Belt Freshman of the Year and a first-team Freshman All-American by The Athletic."}]}}